{"author":{"id":"40e3ba2788b3b9fc163c354afc44e5f9d225bcf0a27e679aaa878dd6135c6dcb"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1777790095,"nonce":"5o7TsvjtUIrJ2JvcvLZ9sc7boO0=","title":"Outreach: Show HN / Lobsters writeup of UC2 v3 revival","message":"Highest-leverage credibility/discovery move available. Single 800-1500 word writeup that earns the cultural capital, then submitted to multiple venues.\n\nAngle: 'Reviving UltraCompressor II: from 1992 DOS to modern C99 with byte-level archive compatibility.' The lineage (de Vries → Bezemer 2015 → Bobrowski 2020 → Valetov 2026) is the hook — multi-decade preservation chains are exactly what HN/Lobsters readers respond to.\n\nRequired content:\n- Brief history of UC2 in the DOS shareware/archiver era (compete with PKZIP, ARJ, RAR; advanced master-block dedup ahead of its time)\n- The lineage chain with proper credit\n- Demonstration: round-trip a 1992 archive with the original UC2 Pro binary in DOSBox-X, then with UC2 v3 — show byte-identical output. Screenshot or asciinema recording.\n- The new compression engine: rANS levels 6-9, CDC + Merkle DAG, BLAKE3 — what's modern about it\n- The DJGPP DOS build target — it still runs on the era it was born in\n- License chain (depends on issue #license-audit being done first)\n- Roadmap teaser: post-quantum, IPFS, ZK proofs (phase 5-9 issues)\n\nSubmission venues, in order:\n1. Lobste.rs (compression, retrocomputing tags) — best-aligned audience\n2. HN Show HN — broader reach, less hostile than r/programming\n3. r/retrobattlestations or r/dos — niche but on-topic\n4. comp.compression USENET (separate issue)\n5. FreeDOS mailing list\n6. vogons.org software-development forum\n\nGating: license audit issue must be closed first (any LGPL/GPL question in HN comments will derail discussion).","files":null}]}